From: Jacob Cook <jacobmcook1984@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sunxi-mmc: Mask DATA0 when updating the clock on H616 eMMC

The H616 eMMC controller has no configuration of its own and matches
the A100 eMMC fallback, which leaves DATA0 unmasked while the clock is
updated. Commit 16e821e3ba47 ("mmc: sunxi: Mask DATA0 when updating the
clock") added the mask because without it subsequent commands time out,
and the H616 SD controllers already set it. Allwinner's sun50iw9 BSP
masks DATA0 on this controller as well.

On the Anbernic RG34XX and RG35XX H this controller drives the second
SD slot. After s2idle the card can hold DATA0 busy while the host
restores its clock; the update times out with STAS 0x606 and the card
is dropped.

Give the H616 eMMC controller its own configuration with mask_data0.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
---
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
@@ -1190,6 +1190,14 @@
 	.needs_new_timings = true,
 };
 
+static const struct sunxi_mmc_cfg sun50i_h616_emmc_cfg = {
+	.idma_des_size_bits = 13,
+	.idma_des_shift = 2,
+	.can_calibrate = true,
+	.mask_data0 = true,
+	.needs_new_timings = true,
+};
+
 static const struct sunxi_mmc_cfg sun50i_h616_cfg = {
 	.idma_des_size_bits = 16,
 	.idma_des_shift = 2,
@@ -1218,6 +1226,7 @@
 	{ .compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-a100-mmc", .data = &sun20i_d1_cfg },
 	{ .compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-a100-emmc", .data = &sun50i_a100_emmc_cfg },
 	{ .compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-h616-mmc", .data = &sun50i_h616_cfg },
+	{ .compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-h616-emmc", .data = &sun50i_h616_emmc_cfg },
 	{ /* sentinel */ }
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, sunxi_mmc_of_match);
